# InEngine Core — PHP and package standards

- For InEngine Core and packages in `../Modules/*`, use PHP `^8.5`.
- Follow PSR standards and Laravel/PHP community style guides.
- Use Laravel Pint for formatting PHP changes.
- Test every code change with Pest (smallest relevant scope first, then broader suite when needed).
- Keep package `composer.json` constraints aligned with Core when compatibility allows.
- Prefer Modulus-compatible modules over app-local feature code for reusable capabilities.
- User/auth belongs in a future Users module — do not reintroduce default Laravel `User` into Core.
